{
  "$schema": "https://developer.microsoft.com/json-schemas/fabric/item/report/definition/visualContainer/2.0.0/schema.json",
  "name": "p6_text",
  "position": {
    "x": 20,
    "y": 10,
    "z": 1000,
    "width": 1240,
    "height": 700,
    "tabOrder": 1000
  },
  "visual": {
    "visualType": "textbox",
    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "2.4.2 Insights",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "20pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#14213D"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "1. Most variants are still unknown (Chart 1). 54.7% of labeled variants are uncertain (VUS); only 8.6% are pathogenic and 32.5% benign.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "2. A few genes dominate (Chart 2). TTN (6,134), BRCA2 (5,779), NF1 (5,740), BRCA1 (4,330) and ATM (3,908) have the most pathogenic variants.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "3. Uncertainty grows faster than answers (Chart 3). Reviews rose from ~33K variants (2017) to ~1.37M (2025); VUS grew from 13K to 878K while pathogenic grew from 9K to 73K.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "4. Most variants have no second opinion (Chart 4). 77.5% are reported by only one lab (median = 1, max = 97).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "5. Bigger genes have more disagreement (Chart 5). Across 7,280 genes with 100+ variants, the rank correlation between size and conflict rate is 0.68; BRCA2 (26.4%) and BRCA1 (21.6%) stand out.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "6. Big DNA changes are easier to judge (Chart 6). Deletions are 60.7% pathogenic; single-letter changes (SNVs) are only 4.9% pathogenic and 57.4% uncertain.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "7. Expert review is rare (Chart 7). 77.6% of variants have 1 star (one lab); only 0.49% were checked by an expert panel or guideline.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "8. Cancer leads the conditions (Chart 8). 'Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome' is linked to ~22,600 pathogenic variants, far ahead of the next ('Inborn genetic diseases', ~7,200).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "9. Cleaning was essential. Without the GRCh38 filter every count would be doubled; 104 label spellings would split the charts; 45% of conditions hide behind 'not provided'.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Numbers are from the ClinVar November 2026 release with all slicers cleared. These are patterns in a public database, not medical advice.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "drillFilterOtherVisuals": true
  }
}
